invariant: INV-16
file: widemul.h
catches: widemul_runtime_test
reason: widemul_answer reads CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES in place of
  CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY, so a caller that stated the AES
  instructions' timing alone runs the native multiply, which nothing
  stated, and one that stated the multiply alone runs the decomposition.
  A session with both bits or neither behaves the same, so the loops that
  set both miss it. bin/widemul_runtime_test requires the answer to
  follow the multiply bit alone.

--- old
    return (cfg->cpu & CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY) != 0 ? WIDEMUL_CONSTANT_TIME
--- new
    return (cfg->cpu & CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES) != 0 ? WIDEMUL_CONSTANT_TIME
